.TH "OSTRYA\-CAT" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-cat \- Write the content of files of a commit to stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya cat [OPTIONS] [COMMIT] [PATH]...
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write the content of files of a commit to stdout.
.PP
The command writes the bytes of each PATH in order, with no separator. It follows a symlink in the last component of a PATH. A directory, or a PATH that names nothing, is an error.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fICOMMIT\fR
The commit to read (a checksum or a ref).
.IP
COMMIT and at least one PATH are required.
.TP
\fIPATH...\fR
The paths to write, in order. A leading \fB\%/\fR is optional.
.IP
Each PATH must name a regular file, or a symlink that leads to one. The command follows a symlink in the last component, up to \%256 links. A symlink in another component is an error. A \fB\%\&.\fR or \fB\%\&..\fR component names nothing. The command stops at the first PATH that fails, and the content of the paths before it stays written.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
